runs/phase1A/day024_chemical_end_rim_design/01_r2_parent_rim_chemical_audit/r2_preliminary_chemical_candidate_classes.csv:2:C0_SIMPLE_EDGE_PASSIVATION_ONLY,Attempt to passivate the existing degree-1 polar BN termini using only small terminal groups.,"Small-group BN edge passivation is chemically plausible in general, but the accepted parent sites are degree 1 rather than conventional degree-2 edge sites.",Insufficient as a direct R2-cap replacement because it neither reproduces the required inward radial closure of 0.779423 nm nor by itself resolves the full parent-side coordination deficit.,0,REJECT_AS_STANDALONE_CAP_REPLACEMENT,Leaves a pore much wider than the validated 0.84 nm aperture and may leave the degree-1 polar termini chemically under-resolved.,10.1021/jp805790s; 10.1039/C9NA00530G
