C0_SIMPLE_EDGE_PASSIVATION_ONLY,Attempt to passivate the existing degree-1 polar BN termini using only small terminal groups.,"Small-group BN edge passivation is chemically plausible in general, but the accepted parent sites are degree 1 rather than conventional degree-2 edge sites.",Insufficient as a direct R2-cap replacement because it neither reproduces the required inward radial closure of 0.779423 nm nor by itself resolves the full parent-side coordination deficit.,0,REJECT_AS_STANDALONE_CAP_REPLACEMENT,Leaves a pore much wider than the validated 0.84 nm aperture and may leave the degree-1 polar termini chemically under-resolved.,10.1021/jp805790s; 10.1039/C9NA00530G
C1_LINKED_BN_ANNULAR_NANOFLAKE,Coaxial atomically thin BN annular nanoflake placed at the validated cap plane and attached through end-specific junction networks: one for the B-terminated lower rim and one for the N-terminated upper rim.,Preserves the BN material family and permits H or mixed edge passivation.,Closest atomistic analogue to the validated planar annular steric cap; estimated monolayer population 145.1 atoms/end.,1,ADVANCE_TO_EXPLICIT_GEOMETRY_AND_JUNCTION_DESIGN,"B-end and N-end linker chemistry, charge compensation, and junction strain must be resolved independently; a direct 90-degree seamless sp2 seam is not assumed.",10.1021/jp805790s; 10.1039/C9NA00530G
C2_RIGID_ORGANIC_OR_HYBRID_MACROCYCLE,"Rigid aromatic or heteroaromatic annulus with an approximately 0.84 nm central pore, multiply anchored to the BNNT rim.",Covalent amine and organic functionalization of BNNTs is documented.,"Potentially synthetically modular, but requires explicit anchor placement and force-field parameterization.",2,ADVANCE_AS_FALLBACK_CANDIDATE_CLASS,"Greater dielectric, dipolar, and electronic perturbation near the lumen.",10.1021/ja063653+
C3_INWARD_TETHERED_FUNCTIONAL_CORONA,Multiple inward-pointing tethered aromatic or polar groups attached around the terminal BN rim.,Uses established covalent BNNT functionalization concepts.,Can reduce the effective aperture but does not naturally reproduce the rigid planar exclusion surface.,3,DEFER_UNLESS_RIGID_ANNULAR_CANDIDATES_FAIL,"Flexibility, pore intermittency, collapse, and strong hydration dependence.",10.1021/ja063653+
C4_METAL_OR_SPIN_ACTIVE_CAP,Metal-coordinated or radical-containing terminal annulus.,Potentially realizable in a broader device architecture.,Outside the current minimal-perturbation confinement gate.,4,REJECT_AT_CURRENT_GATE,Introduces new electronic and spin-active degrees of freedom before they are physically justified.,Not required for current R2 gate

