001789: ### R1
001790: 
001791: R1 remains the neutral frozen closed steric positive control. Its role
001792: is to demonstrate that the confinement-detection method identifies
001793: stable lumen hydration when the end boundary is closed.
001794: 
001795: R1 is not promoted as a chemically realizable architecture.
001796: 
001797: ### R2
001798: 
001799: R2 is the symmetric partial-cap screening architecture. It introduces a
001800: central aperture while maintaining a highly hydrated lumen and allowing
001801: measurable exchange.
001802: 
001803: R2 is also not yet chemically realizable because its cap is represented
001804: by ideal neutral frozen steric beads.
001805: 
